<title>USA: MBIA qualifies nine muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies nine muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. said Monday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal isssues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Des Moines, Iowa, $14.45 million general obligations bonds.</p>
<p>--Waverly, Iowa, $2.45 million Corpororate Purpose GOs.</p>
<p>--Leawood, Kan., $6.945 million GOs bonds.</p>
<p>--Byron Center Public School District, Mich., $5.73 milion school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Ferndale School District, Mich., $16.325 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Farmington, Minn., $2.14 million water revenue GOs.</p>
<p>--Rio Rancho School District No. 94, N.M., $9.8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Bethleham Twp., Pa., $3.665 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Susquenita SD, Pa., $5.395 million GOs, alternate bidding.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
